    feat: prove a node checkout matches origin/main and name the drift — CF-244
    
    A node's clone printed PASS at every layer while it sat one commit behind
    origin/main, because nothing measured the checkout's git state. Measured on
    cf-node (bunker-las-03) before this change: HOME=/home/bunker-cf-node,
    $HOME/repo on main at 7f22d02, tree clean, 1 behind origin/main 04fc398 —
    invisible to verify-node.sh, which graded the agent, the gateway and the auth
    gate and never the tree the node would actually work.
    
    - scripts/node_freshness.py (new, stdlib only): two modes, one classification.
      --workdir measures a local checkout with no bunker, no network and no
      database; --agent/--server resolves the agent's home from the agent and
      measures its clone in ONE bunker exec round trip (the stream dies at 300 s,
      so it is one fast read-only battery). Four arms each name their measured
      value — branch, worktree, ancestor, sync — and the check fails on a detached
      HEAD, an uncommitted path, a diverged HEAD, or any lag, naming the lag count
      and the differing paths. Exit 0 PASS, 1 drift/dirty, 2 usage/unreachable: an
      unmeasurable node is never a PASS. A checkout with no origin is a named FAIL,
      not a crash.
    - scripts/project-node.sh: layer 40 measures the checkout after the clone,
      using the clone's own copy of the probe when it carries one and a node-side
      inline fallback otherwise, so nothing depends on the control host's scripts
      existing on the node. DIRTY is a WARN naming the paths (the node may be
      mid-task, per specs/NODE.md); DRIFT is a FAIL, because a node working a tree
      that no longer matches origin/main is the failure this row exists for.
      --apply records the measurement on the node: $HOME/.node/freshness.json, and
      layer 90 nests it into node.json.
    - scripts/verify-node.sh: a fifth step folds freshness into VERIFY:, so a node
      that answers HTTP but is behind origin/main can no longer print VERIFY: PASS.
      Live: cf-node now prints FAIL checkout_freshness behind=1 / VERIFY: FAIL (1).
    - specs/NODE.md: manifest `freshness` object, the layer-40 cell, and the
      failure semantics (dirty WARN, drift FAIL, neither repaired silently) —
      AGENTS.md rule 1, changed in the same commit as the script.
    - tests/selftest.sh section 47: a real local origin, with the green arm first
      so a red arm is the check refusing real drift rather than a broken fixture.
      The probe rung gets its own seed and origin: an earlier draft committed the
      probe into the seed the other rungs measure, which advanced their origin and
      turned the dirty arm into drift — a fixture that graded itself.
    - docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md: the §47 mapping row and the derived counts
      (50 arms / 47 numbered / 36 unclaimed, 21 governed), which section 39
      enforces both ways.
    
    Evidence at this tree: python3 -m py_compile scripts/node_freshness.py -> OK;
    bash -n on all three shell files -> OK; bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST:
    PASS (section 47: 13 arms green, including the two arms that must go red);
    bash scripts/boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK (4 warnings); live probe
    scripts/node_freshness.py --agent cf-node --server bunker-las-03 -> FAIL
    sync behind=1 naming .coding-hermes/board/{events,tasks}.jsonl, exit 1, 0.96 s.
    
